From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:55:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: rename simulated/theoretical plot titles to fuller,
 clearer names

- Distribution.plot() (already done in previous commit) and the
  simulated/theoretical 2D plots: collapse mode-dependent titles
  ('Contour Plot'/'2D Density Plot', 'Joint Contour Plot'/'Joint PDF
  Plot') into one name each ('Joint Density (Estimated)', 'Joint
  Probability Density Function') since contour= only changes the
  shading, not what's being shown.
- Impulse/Histogram: drop the normalize=True/False-dependent title
  ('Relative Frequency Impulse Plot'/'Count Impulse Plot',
  'Density Histogram'/'Count Histogram') in favor of one name each.
- Density Curve -> Density (Estimated); Segmented Density Plot ->
  Conditional Density (Estimated); Segmented Histogram -> Conditional
  Histogram; 2-D Histogram -> Joint Histogram; Joint PMF Plot -> Joint
  Probability Mass Function.
- make_tile: title is 'Tile Plot' only when both axes are genuinely
  discrete; a mixed (one axis binned) tile is titled 'Joint Histogram'
  instead of claiming to tile discrete cells on both sides.
- Update PLOT_DISPLAY_NAME and CLAUDE.md's stale note about the
  now-collapsed 2D density title/suggestion-note split.
- Update every affected literal-title assertion in test_plot.py.
